==Trivia==
*Moodist Beach may be derived from ''moodiest'' (the most prone to sudden or frequent changes in mood, i.e., Moodist Beach's highly varied stages make it one of the "moodiest" [[Uncanny Legends]] sub-chapters), ''mudar'' (a Portuguese word meaning "to change") and ''nudist beach'' (the joke being that people here are "in the mood" rather than "in the nude").
*Most of the stages' names relate to the enemies appearing in them:
**[[Stars in the Tumbler]] consists mainly of [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]].
**[[Don't Rush Love]] contains [[Teacher Bun Bun]] and [[Bun Bun Black]], whose descriptions both mention "love".
**[[Tear-Soaked Puppy]] introduces [[Li'l Doge]], who is struggling to help [[Doge]]. "Tear-Soaked" may also be a reference to [[Zollow]]'s Japanese description, which mentions acidic tears he has from the pain of his body being stripped of flesh.
**The word ''shinobi'' (忍び) in [[Shinobi Showdown]] exclusively refers to a male ninja in English, but can also mean general stealth or incognito travelling in Japanese. This may hint at how the stage contains [[Assassin Bear]] and [[Doge Dark]], as assassins are expected to be stealthy.
**[[Ancient Sea Blues]] introduces [[Golem Sunfish]], a [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] that was sealed at the bottom of the ocean by a sage.
*Tear-Soaked Puppy is the last Uncanny Legends stage to have no Relics.
*All [[Uncanny Legends]] stages from Shinobi Showdown onward contain Relics.

